---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Email Design"
  description="Author structured email content in Varve's dedicated Email workspace, inspect responsive browser previews, run compatibility checks, and export HTML."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <article class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Email Design
      </nav>
      <h1 class="site-page-title">A workspace for email authoring</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Email uses structured content blocks, responsive preview, semantic markup, and email-focused
        checks. Those constraints give it a dedicated workspace while keeping its artwork in the
        same Varve document model.
      </p>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Author, inspect, and export</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Start from email-aware content blocks and retain authored source alongside rendered content.</li>
          <li>Find saved code blocks even when they have no visible canvas object, and edit their source explicitly.</li>
          <li>Preview responsive layouts in Varve's browser renderer and run email compatibility checks before export.</li>
          <li>Review generated HTML and plain text separately from custom HTML/CSS and authored source.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Sample personalization values are for preview only; they are not silently inserted into
          exported content. Switching to Email does not convert existing artwork or enable an email
          profile automatically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-note">
        <h2>What the preview verifies</h2>
        <p>
          The preview is rendered in Varve's browser surface. It is not a live Gmail or Outlook
          rendering test, and export does not send campaigns or authenticate with an email service
          provider. Review the generated output in your delivery workflow before sending.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p><a href={sitePath('/features/workspaces')}>Explore all six workspaces</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .feature-intro { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 1rem 0 3rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .feature-section { margin: 0 0 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-section p, .feature-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .feature-section li + li { margin-top: .65rem; }
  .feature-note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
